I walk over to a table in the shop.
There are many things on the table.
I am not wearing a scarf today.
I am very cold around my neck.
I see a blue scarf.
It is a very long scarf.
It is made of wool.
I take the blue scarf.
I put it around my neck.
It feels wonderfully warm.
"It is a nice colour," the shop assistant says.
"Yes, and it is very soft," I say.
I look at the price tag.
It costs one hundred and fifty kroner.
It is a good price for a warm scarf.
I take it off again.
"I am buying it too," I say to her.
I put the blue scarf together with the red sweater.
